# Keep the Docker build context small and reproducible: the image builds the app from source with
# Gradle, so local build outputs, caches, VCS, IDE, node_modules, and docs are not needed.
.git
.gitignore
.gradle
**/.gradle
build
**/build
.idea
*.iml
doc
# The OpenTofu definition of the cloud setup is not an image input.
infra
*.log
# Match .gitignore's deploy*.env wildcard: keep every deploy env file (deploy.env, deploy.prod.env, ...) out
# of the image build context (.gcloudignore decides what `gcloud builds submit` uploads to Cloud Build; this
# file trims the docker build inside it and a local `docker build`). Secrets live in Secret Manager, but these
# files must never enter the image regardless.
deploy*.env
.env
# Host-generated frontend dirs (the Gradle build runs npm itself, so none of these are inputs). node_modules
# alone is hundreds of MB of build context that would otherwise be uploaded on every build.
**/node_modules
frontend/dist
frontend/.angular
frontend/coverage
frontend/coverage-e2e
frontend/playwright-report
frontend/test-results
